WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.960
 So today was our first all-partners event.

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:06.520
 We've done a lot of work in groups on

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:07.960
 Zoom, in person,

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:09.800
 and this was an opportunity for us

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:12.430
 to bring everyone together, put everyone

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:13.080
 in a room,

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.080
 because we've got such great expertise,

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.650
 such great community experts, clinical

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:19.200
 experts.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.480
 And the goal of today's event

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:22.720
 is really to put everyone in a room and

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:23.280
 learn.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.040
 Not only learn about Live Healthy Chicago

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.240
 and the work that we're doing,

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:28.840
 but really learn from each other.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:32.180
 We're hoping to be a coalition for

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:34.000
 Chicago by Chicago,

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.040
 that we can put Chicagoans

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:38.260
 who are doing this great work in a room,

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:41.200
 de-silo this from our own institutions,

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.960
 even within our institution,

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:45.060
 from our own clinical practice,

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:48.540
 and look across and see what someone else

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:49.080
 is doing,

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.160
 seeing how else is innovating.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:54.720
 So today we heard from our commissioner

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:55.300
 of public health,

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:58.080
 Dr. Garth Walker, who shared with us

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.320
 not only his personal experience as a

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:00.880
 Chicagoan

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:02.720
 and how he got where he was going,

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:05.020
 but his vision for what Chicago could go

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:05.520
 next.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:07.360
 We heard from Dr. David Ansell,

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:09.680
 who spoke about how Live Healthy Chicago

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:11.770
 kind of came together and could have

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:12.560
 fallen apart

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:15.280
 when funding ended, but didn't, right?

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:16.760
 That everyone at the table made the

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:18.200
 active decision

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:21.760
 to stay, to make the shift, to think

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:22.560
 creatively,

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:25.330
 to put their own opportunities and

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:26.520
 funding on the line,

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:29.940
 to de-silo what is historically

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:31.680
 competitors work, right?

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:34.060
 One hospital does well, another hospital

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.040
 needs to do better.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:37.160
 And so when we sit at a table together,

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:39.260
 we are looking to innovate,

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:41.220
 regardless of the institution that we're

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:41.480
 from,

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:42.920
 which is such a blessing

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:45.680
 and is truly how public health is done.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:49.240
 So we also then did a round table, TED

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:50.680
 Talk style,

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:53.230
 a brief five minutes from a variety of

00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:53.920
 speakers

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:56.000
 on the themes of trust, access, and

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:56.640
 capacity.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:58.620
 Our community advisory board has really

00:01:58.620 --> 00:01:59.160
 bubbled up

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:02.720
 those three themes as challenges, but

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:04.080
 also opportunities.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:05.630
 And we saw it, we have a lot of

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:06.280
 opportunities

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:08.320
 with Live Healthy Chicago to build out

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:09.960
 each of those themes

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:11.630
 in a way that is meaningful and

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:12.360
 thoughtful

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:14.400
 and moves the needle towards a healthier

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.040
 Chicago.

